cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite this repository and the
  experimental / methods papers it wraps.
title: "Pocket Atlas: NMR-timescale dynamics as a prior for cryptic ligandable sites"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Snow
    given-names: Eric
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/snowe36/ai-struct-drugabbility"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible toolkit asking whether NMR-timescale dynamic residues
  (Dyna-1 / RelaxDB-CPMG) spatially coincide with cryptic ligandable sites
  on TEM-1 and KRAS, with an optional long-MD arm on public VP35 FAH/FAST
  trajectories. Dyna-1 predicts where micro-millisecond motion occurs; it
  does not generate molecular dynamics trajectories.
keywords:
  - cryptic pockets
  - NMR dynamics
  - structure-based drug design
  - TEM-1
  - KRAS
  - VP35
